  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/dc28d78d3f9334aad287ba8e3532b95e4287b84b395d58301016bb056dff2006.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=\u03a6(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>-0.86).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/07d788a65e5a5c177e7d1e54a3212c71eb0b36f22ec9f582ebb3ad37c6de8cb7.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<0.86).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/abdde6b554257a3ed44d091a9a87095af7bde7534b0695f5ac97d6bf24bcb160.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>-0.86)=P(Z<0.86)=\u03a6(0.86)=0.8051.\n$$",
